{"condition": "9_engine_v2_full", "prompt_id": "t_qa_06", "category": "direct_qa", "instruction": "What is the theory of evolution by natural selection?", "response": "The theory of evolution by natural selection is a scientific theory that explains how species change over time. It is based on the idea that organisms with traits that are better suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on those advantageous traits to their offspring. Over many generations, this process leads to the development of new species and the extinction of others.\n\nThe theory of evolution by natural selection was first proposed by Charles Darwin in his book \"On the Origin of Species\" in 1859. Darwin's theory was based on his observations of the natural world and his own experiments with animals in captivity. He observed that many species of animals and plants have traits that are better suited to their environment, such as the beak shape of a bird that feeds on insects or the coloration of", "raw_text": " The theory of evolution by natural selection is a scientific theory that explains how species change over time. It is based on the idea that organisms with traits that are better suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on those advantageous traits to their offspring. Over many generations, this process leads to the development of new species and the extinction of others.\n\nThe theory of evolution by natural selection was first proposed by Charles Darwin in his book \"On the Origin of Species\" in 1859. Darwin's theory was based on his observations of the natural world and his own experiments with animals in captivity. He observed that many species of animals and plants have traits that are better suited to their environment, such as the beak shape of a bird that feeds on insects or the coloration of", "n_new_tokens": 160, "stop_reason": "max_tokens", "stop_string": null, "prompt_tokens": 14, "latency_s": 3.8325661