{"condition": "9_engine_v2_full", "prompt_id": "t_cd_02", "category": "code_and_sql", "instruction": "Write a Python function called is_prime(n) that returns True if n is a prime number and False otherwise.", "response": "Here's how you can implement the is_prime function in Python:\n\n```python\ndef is_prime(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```\n\nThis function first checks if the number is less than or equal to 1, in which case it returns False. Then it iterates from 2 to the square root of n (inclusive) and checks if n is divisible by any of these numbers. If it is, the function returns False. If no divisors are found, the function returns True, indicating that n is a prime number.", "raw_text": " Here's how you can implement the is_prime function in Python:\n\n```python\ndef is_prime(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```\n\nThis function first checks if the number is less than or equal to 1, in which case it returns False. Then it iterates from 2 to the square root of n (inclusive) and checks if n is divisible by any of these numbers. If it is, the function returns False. If no divisors are found, the function returns True, indicating that n is a prime number.", "n_new_tokens": 150, "stop_reason": "eos", "stop_string": null, "prompt_tokens": 26, "latency_s": 3.5994467079872265, "ms_per_token": 23.99631138658151, "stop_events": [{"t": 13, "score": 0.3211}, {"t": 14, "score": 0.0743}, {"t": 16, "score": 0.038}, {"t": 21, "score": 0.0842}, {"t": 28, "score": 0.0092}, {"t": 32, "score": 0.1069}, {"t": 45, "score": -0.0312}, {"t": 51, "score": 0.0107}, {"t": 60, "score": 0.1103}, {"t": 64, "score": 0.223}, {"t": 68, "score": 0.4608}, {"t": 69, "score": 0.4766}, {"t": 70, "score": 0.5102}, {"t": 93, "score": 0.3473}, {"t": 121, "score": 