{"condition": "9_engine_v2_full", "prompt_id": "t_cd_05", "category": "code_and_sql", "instruction": "Write a JavaScript function called sumArray that returns the sum of an array of numbers.", "response": "Here's a JavaScript function that returns the sum of an array of numbers:\n\n```javascript\nfunction sumArray(arr) {\n  let sum = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n    sum += arr[i];\n  }\n  return sum;\n}\n```\n\nYou can use this function by passing an array of numbers as an argument, like this:\n\n```javascript\nconst numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\nconst total = sumArray(numbers);\nconsole.log(total); // Output: 15\n```\n\nThis function uses a for loop to iterate over each element in the array and adds it to the sum variable. Finally, it returns the sum of all the numbers in the array.", "raw_text": " Here's a JavaScript function that returns the sum of an array of numbers:\n\n```javascript\nfunction sumArray(arr) {\n  let sum = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n    sum += arr[i];\n  }\n  return sum;\n}\n```\n\nYou can use this function by passing an array of numbers as an argument, like this:\n\n```javascript\nconst numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\nconst total = sumArray(numbers);\nconsole.log(total); // Output: 15\n```\n\nThis function uses a for loop to iterate over each element in the array and adds it to the sum variable. Finally, it returns the sum of all the numbers in the array.", "n_new_tokens": 158, "stop_reason": "eos", "stop_string": null, "prompt_tokens": 21, "latency_s": 3.8276305840117857, "ms_per_token": 24.22551002539105, "stop_events": [{"t": 15, "score": 0.3713}, {"t": 16, "score": 0.1185}, {"t": 18, "score": 0.1378}, {"t": 24, "score": 0.0789}, {"t": 31, "score": 0.0677}, {"t": 48, "score": 0.0761}, {"t": 54, "score": 0.2135}, {"t": 56, "score": 0.2285}, {"t": 60, "score": 0.3425}, {"t": 61, "score": 0.4219}, {"t": 62, "score": 0.4825}, {"t": 63, "score": 0.5186}, {"t": 81, "score": 0.3007}, {"t": 82, "score": 0.1059}, {"t": 8